---
name: delegate-github
description: Delegate tasks requiring repository state, pull requests, issues, or GitHub actions to an isolated subagent. Prefer delegation over granting MCP access to the current agent to prevent context bloat.
compatibility: opencode
---

## Delegation Policy
Use this skill whenever you need to read PRs, issues, repository workflows, or perform git actions.
The parent agent MUST NOT request MCP access directly. All interaction must be delegated.

## Execution Rules
1. Delegate this task using OpenCode's `@mention` system (e.g., `@git-worker` or `@general`).
2. Explicitly instruct the subagent to enable EXACTLY ONE tool: `mcp/github-mcp`.
3. Pass the payload envelope below to the subagent.

## Subagent Injection Payload
Include this exact structure in your delegation message:

Required Tool: mcp/github-mcp
Task Prompt: 
"""
ROLE: Specialized GitHub Worker.
TASK: [Insert specific repo, PR number, or issue to evaluate]

RULES:
1. You may use exactly ONE tool: mcp/github-mcp.
2. Do not explain your reasoning. Produce only the requested artifact.
3. Maximum response size: 500 tokens, max 10 bullet points.

OUTPUT FORMAT:
Status: SUCCESS | NOT_FOUND | ERROR
Summary: [Concise summary of the PR, issue, or repository state]
References: [Links to PRs or commits]
Minimal Code: [Only if reviewing specific lines]
"""
